WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Take a battery and three
resistors in one loop.

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.290
Start at the negative terminal,
and call the potential zero.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.330
Cross the battery, and the
potential jumps up by 12 volts.

4
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.020
Cross each resistor, and it falls.

5
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.550
Along each wire, it stays flat.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.390
Arrive back at the start:
zero again, exactly.

7
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.760
Why must the rises and
drops always cancel?

8
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.980
In this mission, you'll apply the loop
rule to circuits where one resistor sits

9
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.890
in two loops at once.

10
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.870
Then you'll find out what a short circuit,

11
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.390
or a real ammeter or voltmeter,
does to the rest of the circuit.

12
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.430
Your mission: explain why the rises
and drops in potential always cancel,

13
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.920
all the way around a loop.
